[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"489","stub":{"id":"489","section":"Sunrise/Hendricks Road to Flint","altname":"","river":"Lazer Creek","difficulty":"ItoII","states":["USA-GEO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":null,"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Park and carry on the river right side of the bridge. The surrounding area has been decorated with no trespassing signs, which appears to coincide with recent purchases of adjacent property tracts by fishing/hunting businesses. The DNR have been notified that the signs are located in the public right-of-way beside the road.","id":"108618","location":{"latitude":"32.772822","longitude":"-84.473715"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"other","description":"Big Lazer Creek WMA land begins here and continues on river right for the remainder of the run.","id":"7kMUkrjxTtGPzcTH6pubI","location":{"latitude":"32.778714","longitude":"-84.452534"},"name":"WMA boundary (public land begins here)","distance":"1.9","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"DNR access point at river mile 0.1 just upstream of the Flint confluence","id":"113854","location":{"latitude":"32.807998","longitude":"-84.404278"},"name":"Take Out #1 just above the Flint River confluence","distance":"8.84","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"The second of the two developed DNR take-outs, this one is on the Flint 0.8 miles downstream of confluence. It adds one mile of brisk smoothwater paddling beyond Take Out #1 and saves one mile of driving.","id":"BeHVmDObywE6ErQBG2T8d","location":{"latitude":"32.801144","longitude":"-84.396678"},"name":"Take-out #2, on the Flint River, 0.8 miles downstream of the confluence","distance":"9.86","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"**Drive here first** via Google directions. Then continue on to either of the two take-outs. Google doesn't know the road continues past this point.","id":"goHP30NzdPTu0z1LNCQht","location":{"latitude":"32.7982","longitude":"-84.40418"},"name":"Road to the two take-outs","distance":null,"photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"other","description":"Drive here second. **Don't ask Google how to get here.** As the sign indicates, this fork in the shuttle route goes one way toward take-out #1 near the confluence. The other way goes toward take-out #2 on the Flint River.\n\nIt's vital to note that **Google Maps does not give proper directions to this point**. Google will tell you to park on the wrong side of the Flint and swim here.","id":"rG7ALklYVYLKXZEh8vbQu","location":{"latitude":"32.8003","longitude":"-84.3988"},"name":"Fork in the shuttle road","distance":null,"photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Largest rapid","id":"ufgQ2Q9Q4ORUmUpqfM0cg","location":{"latitude":"32.8027","longitude":"-84.4351"},"name":"Coleoatchee Creek rapid","distance":null,"difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"12291"},{"type":"access","description":"This might be an alternative to the Sunrise Rd bridge put-in that becomes useful if landowners between the bridge and the start of WMA land restrict passage.\n\nLocated 2.5 miles downstream of Sunrise Rd bridge, at river mile 6.5.\n\nThe road might be gated for some or all of the year.\n\n**Driving directions**\n\n1\\) Use google to navigate to 32.7799, -84.4358 on Bunkham Road.  \n2\\) Turn left there onto St Joe road  \n3\\) Drive northeast on St Joe road 0.8 miles  \n4\\) Turn left onto a side road at 32.7856, -84.4476  \n5\\) Drive westward 0.6 miles to end of the road at 32.7834, -84.4564  \n6\\) Park. Follow the trail westward 0.17 miles (300 yards) to the river","id":"z16N042UW6hqTkR1AfB3d","location":{"latitude":"32.78235","longitude":"-84.45906"},"name":"Prospective put-in inside the WMA (unconfirmed)","distance":null,"photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"12291","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4347","description":"","caption":"Lazer Creek","poi_name":"Big Shoals","subject":"Suzanne Welander","author":"tw","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/12291","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/12291"}},{"id":"12298","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5009","description":"","caption":"Lazer Creek-small","poi_name":"Big Shoals","subject":"Suzanne Welander\t ","author":"tw","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/12298","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/12298"}}],"detail":{"id":"489","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"This is one of Georgia's prettiest and most remote Fall Line runs. Typical of Fall Line runs that spill over the edge of the Piedmont onto the Coastal Plain, considerable flatwater separates the rapids, of which there are mostly Is and a couple worthwhile IIs. The riverwide stairstep ledge near Coleoatchee Ck confluence might be a III. It's an impressive II+ at the very least. Swims could be long and lumpy but the routes are straight through and recovery (eventual) not a problem.\n\nThe DNR provides two developed take-outs. A fork in the shuttle road (32.8003,-84.3988) has a sign indicating your choice of access points: 'Lazer Ck' and 'Flint River'. The one labeled 'Lazer Ck' is 0.2 miles upstream of the confluence (32.8078,-84.4042). The one labeled 'Flint River' is on the Flint 0.8 miles downstream of the confluence (32.8009,-84.3968). The choice is entirely about whether you want to paddle or drive that last mile.\n\nConsult the WMA map online <https://georgiawildlife.com/big-lazer-creek-wma> because Google Maps doesn't know its way around the WMA roads:","averageGradient":"7","maxGradient":null,"length":"9.9","correlations":[],"pointOfIntere